const IFACE = 'INTERFACE (fixed; every agent of this piece uses exactly this):\n' +
  '  1. FILES. Edited by the builder: ' + CONFTEST + '; ' + GATE_SH + ' (ONLY the csim stage statement, the merge_gate_support.py regression call whose test path is tests/csim, and the transport stage statement, the one whose test path is tests/transport; no other line); ' + REQS + ' (one comment line and one package line). Created by the test writer: ' + NEWTEST + '. NOT created: tests/transport/conftest.py (none exists and none is needed; note that four transport test files import the csim conftest and so run its import-time build in each transport worker: that stays as it is, see the Check). NOT edited: scripts/specfactory/suite_regression.py and merge_gate_support.py (not in the row); suite_regression.parse_pytest and the id parsing are unchanged (xdist prints the same node ids in the short summary).\n' +
  '  2. CONFTEST (' + CONFTEST + '; names fixed). PLACEMENT: every edit goes above the first "# ---- enum mirrors" marker (line 67 today), outside every generated block (sig_table.py and HARNESS-sigblocked police the generated blocks); the guarded call replaces the call at line 57 where it stands, the hook functions go between it and the marker.\n' +
  '     a. _build_libs() keeps its name, arguments, make command (make -s libouroboros.so libouroboros_dbg.so in REPO_ROOT), timeout, BUILD_ERROR text and the removal of the stale libraries on a failed build; ADDED: it removes REPO_ROOT / "libouroboros.so" and REPO_ROOT / "libouroboros_dbg.so" (not LIB_PATH or DBG_LIB_PATH, which may name a session copy). RULED: the module-level call stays at import but is guarded: `if not os.environ.get("OM_CSIM_LIB"): _build_libs()` (so a worker, which inherits OM_CSIM_LIB from the controller, or a caller that supplied the library, builds nothing; every other import, including a script that imports the conftest outside pytest such as scripts/bench_tactical_pipe.py:116 or scripts/specfactory/snapshot_fixture.py:52, and a run with -p no:xdist or -n 0, builds at import exactly as today). _HAS_CSRC stays computed at import.\n' +
  '     b. LIB_PATH is pathlib.Path(os.environ["OM_CSIM_LIB"]) when that variable is set and non-empty, else REPO_ROOT / "libouroboros.so" (today\'s path: a bare pytest tests/csim without xdist is unchanged). RULED: DBG_LIB_PATH is Path(os.environ["OM_CSIM_LIB_DBG"]) when set and non-empty, else REPO_ROOT / "libouroboros_dbg.so"; BUILD_ERROR starts as os.environ.get("OM_CSIM_BUILD_ERROR") or None.\n' +
  '     c. RULED: pytest_configure(config), a hook in the conftest, and the single make call of the controller: a worker (hasattr(config, "workerinput"), that is worker_id present) returns at once and never runs make (its import-time build was skipped because OM_CSIM_LIB was inherited). The controller (no workerinput) has already built once at import (the guarded call of item a, env unset at that moment); ADDED: the hook calls no second make. When OM_CSIM_LIB is already set in the environment at hook time the hook does nothing (the caller supplied the library). When xdist really distributes (worker_id absent and getattr(config.option, "numprocesses", None) is truthy: under -p no:xdist the attribute is absent, -n 0 is falsy, -n auto is a string that is truthy and is never used by the gate; with -p no:xdist or -n 0 the hook does nothing: no directory, no variable, LIB_PATH stays today\'s path), the controller creates the session directory Path(os.environ.get("TMPDIR") or tempfile.gettempdir()) / ("om_csim_" + str(os.getpid())) (the main process id), copies each built library that exists into it with shutil.copy2 under the same file name, and sets os.environ["OM_CSIM_LIB"] to <session dir>/libouroboros.so, os.environ["OM_CSIM_LIB_DBG"] to <session dir>/libouroboros_dbg.so and, when BUILD_ERROR is set, os.environ["OM_CSIM_BUILD_ERROR"] to it (the workers inherit the environment when xdist starts them, after pytest_configure). After a failed build nothing is copied and the two variables still name the session paths (files absent), so each worker fails with the same COMPILE ERROR text as today.\n' +
  '     d. RULED: pytest_unconfigure(config): the controller that made a session directory removes it (shutil.rmtree, ignore_errors=True). A SIGKILL of the controller (a gate timeout) skips it and leaves the om_csim_<pid> directory behind; nothing cleans it up in this piece.\n' +
  '  3. GATE (' + GATE_SH + '; draft names DRAFT-xdist-workers: csim 5, transport 2). The csim statement becomes (options first, then --, then the tests and the flags; ADDED --before-build): "$PYTHON" "$GATE_DIR/merge_gate_support.py" regression "$CANDIDATE" "$BASE_REF" --python "$PYTHON" --timeout "$SUITE_TIMEOUT" --merge-root "$MERGE_ROOT" --before-build "make -s libouroboros.so libouroboros_dbg.so" -- tests/csim -n 5 --dist loadfile -p no:cacheprovider (output redirection to $REG_CSIM_LOG unchanged). If HARNESS-gate-keep-red-evidence has landed (it must have: it is a dependency), its MALLOC_PERTURB_=255 env prefix on these two statements stays exactly as it is. The transport statement keeps its options and its --before-build "make -s pipe/ouroboros_pipe" and ends -- tests/transport -n 2 --dist loadfile -p no:cacheprovider (redirection to $TRANSPORT_LOG unchanged). The strings "-n 5 --dist loadfile -p no:cacheprovider" and "-n 2 --dist loadfile -p no:cacheprovider" each appear exactly once in the file, on those statements; no other stage (tests/qa/t1, tests/specfactory, the lab stage) gets a flag. Each of the two statements carries a one-line comment "# See also: tests/csim/conftest.py pytest_configure (OM_CSIM_LIB): the library is built once by the xdist controller; the flags follow -- because merge_gate_support.py regression takes them as test_args" and the conftest hook points back ("# See also: scripts/specfactory/merge_gate.sh csim stage (-n 5)").\n' +
  '  4. BASELINE. The baseline run (the cache miss) uses the same command as the branch run: merge_gate_support.py regression_check passes the same test_args to the base-tree run and the candidate run, and suite_key = " ".join(test_args), so the changed command is a miss by itself; nothing in merge_gate_support.py or suite_regression.py changes.\n' +
  '  5. REQUIREMENTS (' + REQS + '): a comment line "# pytest-xdist: the merge gate csim and transport stages run pytest -n (merge_gate.sh); install it in the gate venv and in the pre-gate venv." followed by the package line "' + XDIST_REQ + '" (after the PyYAML line).\n' +
  '  6. DETERMINISM (the Check): every csim test must give the same result alone and under --dist loadfile; the whole suite is run once both ways and any test whose verdict differs is a FINDING (an order-dependent test is a real finding, never a skip).\n' +
  '  7. FIXTURE of the test (the test writer picks file names and numbers): a conftest copy under tmp_path (the real tests/csim/conftest.py copied to <tmp>/tests/csim/conftest.py, so its REPO_ROOT = parents[2] is <tmp>) next to 3 fixture test files (3 files so --dist loadfile gives both workers a file), a stub make (an executable named make in a directory put first on PATH: it appends one line "<its parent pid> <arguments>" to the file named by $OM_STUB_COUNT, then, unless $OM_STUB_FAIL is set (it then prints that text to stderr and exits 1), touches libouroboros.so and libouroboros_dbg.so in its cwd), TMPDIR pointed at <tmp>/tmp, OM_CSIM_LIB and the other OM_CSIM_ variables removed from the child environment, pytest run as a subprocess with sys.executable -m pytest -p no:cacheprovider from <tmp> (so the real make is never called and the real repo is never built).'

const ruler = (r) => agent(RULES + '\nRole: ruler (Engineer), rules.md section (e). Builder branch origin/' + r.branch + ' stopped with: ' + r.stop_reason + '\nSpec: ' + SPEC + '.' + SPEC_BLOCK + ' Rulebook: docs/northstar/plans/2026-10-07-visible-game-rulebook.md (its "Decision procedure" word for word). Ledger ' + LEDGER + ': a test-defect gets the row TD-HARNESS-' + K + ' (a new row). Branch push/vg-harness-' + K + '-rulings (suffix vg-harness-' + K + '-rulings; continue it from origin if it exists, else cut it from origin/' + TB + ' so your edit is a delta on the writer\'s file). If every condition of the procedure holds: edit only the one test file named, run it alone and its positive control, append the ledger row, push, report ruled true with row and branch. Else report ruled false and brief (under one page: test id and failing line, the builder\'s claim, the spec and brief lines that bear on it, two or three options with what each changes). A threshold, a window, a tolerance, the DRAFT-xdist-workers values, a Westley-owned number, or anything the INTERFACE items fix (names, paths, env variables, the gate statements) is never ruled here: ruled false.', { label: 'rule:' + r.branch, phase: 'Build', schema: RULING, agentType: 'engineer', model: 'sonnet' })
const withRuling = async (mk) => {
  let r = await mk('')
  if (r && !r.ok && /^test-defect:/.test(r.stop_reason || '')) {
    const v = await ruler(r)
    if (v && v.ruled && v.branch) { r = await mk(', origin/' + v.branch + ' (ruling ' + v.row + ')'); r = { ...r, ruling: v } } else { r = { ...r, ruling: v } }
  }
  return r
}

phase('Preflight')
const pre = await agent(RULES_PRE + '\nRole: read-only scout (Engineer), rules.md section (c); detached worktree of ' + SPEC_REF + ' (git fetch first; give its sha), suffix vg-harness-' + K + '-pre, removed after with git worktree remove (no --force). Spec: ' + SPEC + '.' + SPEC_BLOCK + ' Check and quote each with file:line and the sha read; mark what you did not run as unverified. (1) DEPENDS (blocking): read ' + PIECES_TOML + ' with tomllib; the ids ' + DEPS.join(' and ') + ' must exist and be attached (or landed/done); if any of the four is absent or not attached: blocking true and the first words of evidence are "depends-not-attached: <ids>" (say which are absent from the file and which are queued; quote state and attach_sha of each). (2) ROW (blocking on a difference): the row ' + ROW + ' exists, state queued, owns CONTAINS ' + PRODUCT.join(', ') + ' and ' + NEWTEST + ' (tests/transport/conftest.py may be listed too: report it; it is not needed), depends_on contains all four ids of (1), acceptance contains ' + NEWTEST + ' (quote the row; a missing owned file or dependency is blocking true). owns MUST include ' + REQS + ' (the records edit adds it: if it is absent say so, blocking true). REVERSED EDGES: if depends_on of this row holds any of VG-CONTRACT-layerspot, VG-CONTRACT-route or LAB-REV2-E0 (they must depend ON ' + ROW + ', not the reverse; both directions form a cycle): blocking true, first words of evidence "reversed-edge: <ids>". The row\'s size_estimate must say -n 5 and not -n 6 (quote it; a difference is blocking true, first words "row-text: <what>"). Every id of ' + PIECES + ' exists (quote state and attach_sha of PP-ledger and HARNESS-status). (3) OWNERS: with a python snippet (tomllib, fnmatch over owns and owns_glob) list EVERY other piece that owns or globs ' + PRODUCT.join(', ') + ' or ' + NEWTEST + ' with its state and depends_on (queued, landed and superseded count as in flight; attached does not). Expected (Architect ruling 2026-10-21): VG-E-prodslot (conftest), HARNESS-gate-base-after-lock and HARNESS-gate-keep-red-evidence (merge_gate.sh) are dependencies of this row (ordered, not a block once attached); VG-CONTRACT-layerspot, VG-CONTRACT-route and LAB-REV2-E0 (conftest) take depends_on HARNESS-csim-xdist by a records edit: report for each whether it lists it (NOT blocking); A94-harness (attached, glob scripts/specfactory/[!m]*: ordering only). For any OTHER in-flight owner say whether a depends_on path orders it against ' + ROW + ' in either direction; one without an ordering is blocking true with the first words of evidence "unordered-owner: <ids>". Run ' + PY + ' scripts/specfactory/owner_lint.py --pieces <the pieces.toml> and scripts/specfactory/pieces.py --check and paste the last lines. (4) POSITIVE CONTROL, the base facts (blocking true on a mismatch that changes a brief): ' + NEWTEST + ' does not exist (git ls-tree); ' + CONFTEST + ' has LIB_PATH hardcoded to REPO_ROOT / "libouroboros.so" and the module-level call _build_libs() (quote the lines); ' + GATE_SH + ' has no -n on the tests/csim or tests/transport regression statement and passes --before-build only on the transport one (HARNESS-gate-keep-red-evidence, a dependency, may have added a MALLOC_PERTURB_=255 env prefix to both: say so; quote both statements with line numbers); ' + REQS + ' has no xdist line; tests/transport has no conftest.py; the argparse form of the INTERFACE (options, then --, then tests and flags) is accepted by merge_gate_support.py regression: show it with a python snippet that imports merge_gate_support from the worktree and parses ["regression", "C", "B", "--python", "P", "--", "tests/csim", "-n", "5", "--dist", "loadfile", "-p", "no:cacheprovider"] through its argument parser without running anything (or, if main() cannot be given a dry argv, say unverified). (5) HOST (a plain check, read-only; pytest-xdist 3.8.0 was installed in both venvs by the Dispatcher on 2026-10-21, so it passes; blocking true only if either import fails): run ' + GATE_PY + ' -c "import xdist, pytest, sys; print(xdist.__version__, pytest.__version__, sys.version)" and ' + PY + ' -c "import xdist, pytest; print(xdist.__version__, pytest.__version__)" and paste both outputs, plus nproc. pre_gate.sh runs the new test file with the second interpreter (pre_gate.sh :33), the gate stages with the first (merge_gate.sh :19). Do NOT install anything. (6) BASELINE: run ' + PY + ' -m pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider tests/specfactory once from the worktree (timeout 1800); put the summary line in baseline and every failing id in baseline_red. Do not rerun to hide a flake; list a second run separately. (7) KNOWN RED: print the non-comment lines of scripts/specfactory/gd_tests_known_red.txt and lane_plays_known_red.txt (ids only, count them) into known_red as one string. (8) BRANCHES: run git -C ~/Projects/ouroboros-manifold branch -r | grep -i xdist and ls ~/Projects/om-push/wt | grep -i xdist: both must print nothing (blocking true otherwise). (9) GATE LOCK (informational, never blocking): flock -n ~/Projects/om-push/gate.lock true && echo free; report free or held. (10) SPEC TEXT: if any docs/northstar/plans/*.md on the tree holds the heading "HARNESS-csim-xdist: the sim suites across cores", diff its section against the SPEC SECTION above and report each difference in a number, an owner or a name (blocking true on one). (11) VERIFIED facts V1 to V4 and D1 to D9 of the script header: for each say whether it still matches ' + SPEC_REF + ' (which lines moved); blocking true if a mismatch changes a brief. Report pass, blocking, evidence, sha, baseline, baseline_red, known_red.', { label: 'preflight:' + K, phase: 'Preflight', schema: PREFLIGHT, agentType: 'engineer', model: 'sonnet' })
if (!pre || pre.blocking) return { pre, stopped: (pre && /depends-not-attached/i.test(pre.evidence || '')) ? 'depends-not-attached' : (pre && /reversed-edge/i.test(pre.evidence || '')) ? 'reversed-edge' : (pre && /row-text/i.test(pre.evidence || '')) ? 'row-text' : (pre && /unordered-owner/i.test(pre.evidence || '')) ? 'unordered-owner' : 'preflight' }
let out = { pre }
const BL = 'BASELINE (Preflight, ' + SPEC_REF + ' ' + (pre.sha || '?') + '): ' + (pre.baseline || '(none)') + '; failing ids there: ' + ((pre.baseline_red || []).join(', ') || '(none)') + '. The failing set of tests/specfactory on your tree must equal it plus only this piece\'s own named red tests until built.'
const testFiles = [NEWTEST]

phase('Tests')
const tests = done('tests:' + K) || await agent(RULES + '\nRole: test writer (Engineer), rules.md section (d), for ' + ROW + ': ' + SPEC + '.' + SPEC_BLOCK + ' Branch ' + TB + ', suffix vg-harness-' + K + '-tests, from origin/main. You create ONLY ' + NEWTEST + ' (new). Tests are the spec: one case per sentence of the section and of the INTERFACE below. You are NOT the builder. The file header quotes the SPEC SECTION and INTERFACE items 2 to 5 word for word (method rev 3) and names the ADDED items as the Architect\'s defaults.\n' + IFACE + '\n' + BL + '\nThe file carries a line "# Rule pins: <ids>" in its first 40 lines; this piece proves no bible rule, so write "# Rule pins: none (tooling piece, gate-tiers spec section HARNESS-csim-xdist)". Every case that needs xdist FAILS (not skips) with the message "pytest-xdist missing from <sys.executable>" when import xdist fails (the Preflight guarantees it imports in both venvs).\nCASES (the fixture of INTERFACE 7; every run is a subprocess; read the count file and the per-test record files the fixture tests write): (T1) controller builds once: pytest tests/csim -n 2 --dist loadfile -q on the 3-file fixture gives exactly ONE line in the stub count file (the controller\'s import-time build; the workers inherit OM_CSIM_LIB and skip it), its parent pid equals the pid in the session directory name om_csim_<pid> found under <tmp>/tmp by the fixture tests (record the directory while the run is alive: each fixture test writes os.environ["OM_CSIM_LIB"] and whether that path exists), and that pid is NOT the pid of any worker (each fixture test writes os.getpid() and hasattr(config, "workerinput") through a fixture of the fixture conftest copy or request.config); (T2) a worker loads OM_CSIM_LIB: in every fixture test the module conftest.LIB_PATH equals Path(os.environ["OM_CSIM_LIB"]), lies in a directory named om_csim_<digits> under <tmp>/tmp, is not <tmp>/libouroboros.so, and conftest.DBG_LIB_PATH likewise for OM_CSIM_LIB_DBG; both files exist while the run is alive; (T3) no worker ever runs make: from T1, the count stays 1 with 2 workers and with 3 fixture files on both workers (a run with -n 2 where each of two workers ran at least one test, proven by two distinct pids in the records); (T4) cleanup: after the run the om_csim_<pid> directory is gone from <tmp>/tmp; (T5) a bare run is unchanged: the same fixture with -p no:xdist (and again with -n 0): ONE make call, conftest.LIB_PATH == <tmp>/libouroboros.so (today\'s path), OM_CSIM_LIB and OM_CSIM_LIB_DBG unset in the tests, no om_csim_ directory under <tmp>/tmp; (T6) LIB_PATH reads OM_CSIM_LIB: python -c in a subprocess that loads the fixture conftest by importlib from <tmp>/tests/csim/conftest.py: with OM_CSIM_LIB=/some/dir/x.so set, LIB_PATH == Path("/some/dir/x.so"); unset or empty, LIB_PATH == <tmp>/libouroboros.so; same for OM_CSIM_LIB_DBG and DBG_LIB_PATH; with OM_CSIM_BUILD_ERROR=boom set, BUILD_ERROR == "boom", else None; (T7) the import-time build stays outside pytest (scripts/bench_tactical_pipe.py:116 pattern, also scripts/specfactory/snapshot_fixture.py): a python -c subprocess in <tmp> with env OM_CSIM_LIB unset does sys.path.insert(0, "tests/csim"); import conftest as csim and then csim.LIB_PATH.exists(): the count file has ONE line after the bare import, LIB_PATH == <tmp>/libouroboros.so and exists, csim.load_lib is defined (do not call it: the stub .so files are empty); calling csim._build_libs() by hand runs make once more (count 2); with OM_CSIM_LIB set to an existing file the same import runs no make (count 0) and LIB_PATH is that file; (T7b) the real scripts/bench_tactical_pipe.py still imports the conftest the way T7 does: text case that its ctypes_run function contains "import conftest as csim" and "csim.load_lib()" and nothing in it calls make or sets OM_CSIM_LIB; (T8) a failed build still gives every test the COMPILE ERROR text: with OM_STUB_FAIL=boom, a csrc/x.c in the fixture tree, -n 2: the count file has one line, each fixture test that uses the conftest lib fixture FAILS with a message holding "COMPILE ERROR" and "boom", and no stale libouroboros.so is left in <tmp>; (T9) a caller-supplied OM_CSIM_LIB: with OM_CSIM_LIB set to an existing file in the child environment and -n 2, the count file stays empty (import skips the build, the hook does nothing) and no om_csim_ directory appears; (T9b) -p no:xdist with the same variable set: count empty, LIB_PATH is that file; (T10) the gate lines: read ' + GATE_SH + ' as text; take the shell statement (physical lines joined across trailing backslashes) that contains "merge_gate_support.py" regression and the argument tests/csim: it contains "-- tests/csim -n 5 --dist loadfile -p no:cacheprovider" and the --before-build string "make -s libouroboros.so libouroboros_dbg.so"; the statement with tests/transport contains "-- tests/transport -n 2 --dist loadfile -p no:cacheprovider" and still "--before-build \\"make -s pipe/ouroboros_pipe\\""; the statements for tests/qa/t1 and tests/specfactory contain no " -n "; each flag string appears exactly once in the file; (T11) the parser accepts the new form: merge_gate_support.py regression C B --python P --timeout 9 --merge-root M --before-build X -- tests/csim -n 5 --dist loadfile -p no:cacheprovider yields test_args == ["tests/csim", "-n", "5", "--dist", "loadfile", "-p", "no:cacheprovider"] (import merge_gate_support and call its main with regression_check monkeypatched to record its arguments); (T12) the baseline run uses the same command: with suite_regression.run_pytest monkeypatched to record its test_args argument, merge_gate_support.regression_check on a tmp git repo (init, one commit; candidate_dir that repo, base_ref HEAD, merge_root None) with test_args from T11 calls it twice (base tree, candidate) with an identical list that includes "-n"; (T13) the id parsing is unchanged: run a fixture with 4 tests, one failing, and one erroring in a fixture, once plain and once with -n 2 --dist loadfile, and suite_regression.parse_pytest(stdout) gives the same failing ids tuple (sorted) both times; (T14) the requirements file: ' + REQS + ' has a non-comment line equal to "' + XDIST_REQ + '"; (T15) loadfile keeps a file on one worker: the 3-file fixture records the worker pid per test: all tests of one file share one pid. POSITIVE CONTROLS first, green today on the base tree: (C1) the stub make: called directly it appends exactly one line and creates both .so files; with OM_STUB_FAIL set it exits 1; (C2) a fixture conftest written in the test that reproduces TODAY\'s behaviour (a module-level call that runs make through subprocess at import, the two lines of the base conftest :41 and :57) under -n 2 gives more than one stub line (every process builds: the race of the spec) so the count detector can tell once from many; (C3) the T10 text detector applied to a snippet of TODAY\'s csim statement (copied inline from ' + GATE_SH + ' :295-296) reports the flags missing, and applied to a snippet that has them reports them present; (C4) the fixture-run helper returns a pytest exit code 0 and the per-test records for a trivial passing fixture. Then the RED cases, red for the stated reason on the base tree: the conftest builds at import in every process (more than one stub line under -n 2: every worker builds at import since the base conftest has no OM_CSIM_LIB guard; paste the real count), LIB_PATH ignores OM_CSIM_LIB, the worker path of T2 is the repo-root library, an inherited OM_CSIM_LIB does not stop the build (T9 count is not 0), ' + GATE_SH + ' carries no -n, ' + REQS + ' has no xdist line; T7 and T5 are GREEN controls today (the bare import-time build is unchanged); paste what each reports. Thresholds: none invented; every number is a fixture value, the ruled -n 5 or -n 2, or a count the INTERFACE gives.\nON THE BASE TREE (origin/main, no feature): run ' + NEWTEST + ' and tests/specfactory once; the new cases must be red for the reasons above (paste the failing assertion line of EVERY red test verbatim: file:line and message) and every control green (paste the pytest summary line). Pre-gate: ' + PREGATE('<worktree>', 'origin/main', NEWTEST) + '; red tests make the test step REJECT by design: quote that line and say the other steps are OK. Report ok, branch, sha, summary (failing lines, control lines), red_ids.', { label: 'tests:' + K, phase: 'Tests', schema: REPORT, agentType: 'engineer', model: 'sonnet' })
out = { ...out, tests }
if (!(tests && tests.ok)) return { ...out, stopped: 'tests:' + K }

phase('Build')
const mkBuild = (extra) => done('build:' + K) || agent(RULES + '\nRole: Doer (rules.md section (a)) for ' + ROW + ': ' + SPEC + '.' + SPEC_BLOCK + ' Branch ' + BB + ', suffix vg-harness-' + K + ', from origin/main; merge origin/' + tests.branch + rulingMerge() + extra + '.\nEdit ONLY ' + PRODUCT.join(', ') + ' (the owner row ' + ROW + ' also owns ' + NEWTEST + ': that is the test writer\'s, you never edit it). In ' + GATE_SH + ' touch only the csim and the transport regression statements (a hunk anywhere else stops you). Build exactly the INTERFACE: every name, variable, path and string it gives. Numbers: only DRAFT-xdist-workers (csim 5, transport 2), the 180 s make timeout that already exists, and the INTERFACE; a number or rule neither gives stops you with stop_reason "spec-gap: <what>". If merge_gate_support.py regression refuses the option order of INTERFACE 3, stop with "spec-gap: argument order" (that file is not yours). Comments only where non-obvious: the two "# See also:" lines of INTERFACE 3 and one line in the requirements file; no new docstring; update a docstring sentence only where the change makes it wrong (the _build_libs docstring says any pytest run self-builds: under xdist the controller builds once and the workers load OM_CSIM_LIB). Size: about 40 added lines in the conftest, 8 in merge_gate.sh, 2 in the requirements file; a diff over about 100 lines in total stops you with stop_reason "size: <lines>". STOP (ok=false, stop_reason): a file outside the list above; any test edit; a threshold you would have to change; a lint you would have to disable; a test that looks wrong ("test-defect: ..." form).\n' + IFACE + '\n' + BL + '\nDone when every test of ' + NEWTEST + ' is green with its controls, tests/specfactory fails exactly on the baseline set, python -m py_compile is clean on ' + CONFTEST + ', bash -n ' + GATE_SH + ' is clean, a bare run of one small csim file (cd the worktree; make -s libouroboros.so libouroboros_dbg.so; ' + GATE_PY + ' -m pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider -p no:xdist tests/csim/<one existing small test file>) behaves as on the base tree (same pass/fail counts as the base worktree gives for the same file), and the pre-gate: ' + PREGATE('<worktree>', 'origin/main', NEWTEST) + ' ends PRE_GATE verdict OK; quote it. Report ok, branch, sha, summary (the test lines, every constant, path and variable name you added with its source), red_ids, parked.', { label: 'build:' + K, phase: 'Build', schema: REPORT, agentType: 'doer', model: 'sonnet' })
const build = await withRuling(mkBuild)
out = { ...out, build }
if (!(build && build.ok)) return { ...out, stopped: 'build:' + K }

phase('Check')
const check = SKIP['check:' + K] ? { pass: true, evidence: 'skipped: check ok', findings: [] } : await agent(RULES_PRE + '\nRole: gate checker (Engineer), rules.md section (c), read-only (apart from build outputs and logs under your own directory), detached worktree at origin/' + build.branch + ' (suffix chk-vg-harness-' + K + '; remove it after with git worktree remove, no --force). Spec: ' + SPEC + '.' + SPEC_BLOCK + MEASURE_BLOCK + IFACE + '\n' + BL + '\n(1) SCOPE: the diff versus its merge base touches only ' + PRODUCT.join(', ') + ' plus, from the merged test branch, ' + NEWTEST + '; list every other file (blocking). In ' + GATE_SH + ' print git diff -U0 and show every hunk lies inside the csim or the transport regression statement (blocking otherwise); in the conftest list every added and removed line. (2) Run ' + NEWTEST + ' and the whole tests/specfactory: PASS/FAIL per file with counts; the failing set equals the baseline. (3) POSITIVE CONTROL: in a scratch copy put the three product files back to the base: every red case of ' + NEWTEST + ' goes red again for the stated reason and the controls stay green; list case by case. (4) PRE-GATE line format: run ' + PREGATE('<this worktree>', 'origin/main', NEWTEST) + ' and paste EVERY line; each is "PRE_GATE <step> OK|REJECT|WARN ..." and it must end PRE_GATE verdict OK; list each WARN. (5) DETERMINISM RUN (the spec checker; this is the long step: start it in the BACKGROUND and poll with one foreground command under 10 minutes at a time, every 5 minutes at most). In the worktree: make -s libouroboros.so libouroboros_dbg.so pipe/ouroboros_pipe pipe/ouroboros_pipe_dbg. Then, as ONE background shell script that you write under ~/Projects/om-push/tmp-vg-harness-' + K + '-chk/ (mkdir -p it; TMPDIR=$HOME/Projects/om-push/tmp-vg-harness-' + K + '-chk; run the commands in this order and record date +%s before and after each): (a) cd <worktree> && ' + GATE_PY + ' -m pytest tests/csim -n 5 --dist loadfile -p no:cacheprovider -q --junitxml=<dir>/csim_xdist.xml (timeout 1800); (b) the same with -p no:xdist instead of -n 5 --dist loadfile, junit csim_alone.xml (timeout 4200); (c) tests/transport with -n 2 --dist loadfile, junit transport_xdist.xml (timeout 1800); (d) tests/transport with -p no:xdist, junit transport_alone.xml (timeout 1800). The gate python is ' + GATE_PY + ' (merge_gate.sh :19), the same as the stages. Then compare with a stdlib python script you write in your own directory (not in the repo): from each junit xml take the outcome of every testcase (passed, failed, error, skipped) keyed by classname::name, and print (i) both pass/fail/skip counts, (ii) every id whose outcome differs between alone and loadfile, (iii) ids present in only one run. EVERY differing id is a FINDING: put one line per finding into the findings list, "FINDING: <id> alone=<outcome> xdist=<outcome> first-assertion=<first line of the failure message of the red side>"; re-run each differing id alone (single process) once and once more under -n 2 on its own file and say whether it is order-dependent (verdict follows the neighbours) or flaky (varies by itself); an order-dependent test is a real finding and is never classed as a skip. Also list the ids red in BOTH runs (known red: compare with ' + (pre.known_red || '(the two known-red files)') + ') and any test that is red under xdist with a message naming OM_CSIM_LIB, make, a library path, or "COMPILE ERROR" (blocking true: the piece itself broke it). WALL-CLOCK TESTS (flaky under load; name them in the report): tests/csim/test_E02_gate_drift_trajectory.py:73-77 (0.5 s and 50 us/tick budgets), tests/csim/test_E17_S186_terrain_field.py:182 (terrain generate time limit), tests/csim/test_VG_W_w1_planner.py:469 (DRAFT-walk-tick-ms-w1 minimum of medians): if any is among the ids that differ or is red under xdist, rerun it three times alone and three times while the xdist csim run of step (a) is repeated in the background (under load) and say which of the verdicts follow the load; for ANY id that differs between the runs, repeat the -n 5 --dist loadfile run a second time (timeout 1800, junit csim_xdist2.xml) and list which ids differ in the second run too (a verdict that changes from run to run is flaky, one that is stable is order-dependent). ARGTYPES HAZARD (note it in the report): shared ctypes handles carry argtypes that test modules rebind at module level (about 67 test files do, per the audit; tests/csim/test_B3_C2_friction_golden.py:23 documents the hazard and avoids it with a private function pointer), and which files share a worker varies from run to run, so a failure naming argtypes, ArgumentError or a wrong struct type is a FINDING of this kind. Paste the wall times of the four runs in seconds and the ratio csim alone / csim xdist and transport alone / transport xdist into timings (the measurement report: the csim stage is expected to fall from about 40 minutes to under 10 for the gate with its baseline; the real gate numbers come from the Clerk). If the xdist csim run does not finish within its timeout, or xdist crashes: pass false, blocking true, with the last 40 lines of the log. (5b) TRANSPORT IMPORTERS (D3 as corrected): list the transport files that import the csim conftest (git grep -n "import conftest" tests/transport: test_pipe_wave_spawn.py:49 and :57, test_pipe_shapes.py:63, test_pipe_tactical_world.py:64, test_pipe_mission_cycle.py:108 and :118) and say in which fixtures; show that in a transport session OM_CSIM_LIB is unset and the pytest_configure hook does not run (print os.environ.get in a one-line tmp test or read the code); and show the state of the baseline tree for the transport stage: create a detached worktree of origin/main (suffix chk-vg-harness-' + K + '-base), run make -s pipe/ouroboros_pipe in it exactly as the gate\'s --before-build does and then ls -l libouroboros.so libouroboros_dbg.so there: say whether libouroboros_dbg.so exists after that command (the answer decides the Architect\'s proposal: make the transport --before-build also build libouroboros_dbg.so); remove that worktree after with git worktree remove (no --force). (5c) GATE-RUNNING TESTS: tests/specfactory/test_gate_look_and_times.py:85 and :177-225 and tests/specfactory/test_gate_a94_steps.py:95 run the real merge_gate.sh on scratch repos with a tests/csim fixture, so from now on they execute the xdist command (-n 5 --dist loadfile in a scratch tree); list their pass/fail in the whole tests/specfactory run of step (2) and say whether any failure message names -n, xdist, OM_CSIM_LIB or an unrecognized argument (blocking true if so). (6) NON-PYTEST IMPORTERS (D9, RULED: unchanged): with the worktree built and OM_CSIM_LIB unset, run ' + GATE_PY + ' -c "import sys; sys.path.insert(0, \'tests/csim\'); import conftest as c; print(c.LIB_PATH, c.LIB_PATH.exists(), c.BUILD_ERROR, callable(c.load_lib))" (the scripts/bench_tactical_pipe.py:116 and snapshot_fixture.py patterns: it must print the repo-root path and True without any prior make call by you beyond the worktree build) and show the module-level guarded call in the diff; read-only for the scripts themselves (do not run bench_tactical_pipe.py). (7) STALE DOCS (report only, never edit): git grep -n -i -E "single.process|no xdist|xdist not installed|-p no:cacheprovider tests/csim" over docs/ scripts/ tests/ and list each hit with whether it states something this change makes false (the historical hits of the script header V4 are known). (8) Every constant, string, variable name and rule added in the product diff listed with its source (the section, an INTERFACE item or an ADDED item); blocking true for one with no source; the two "# See also:" lines are present at both sites. (9) WIRED: state what is reachable after this piece: the csim and transport stages of merge_gate.sh run with the flags on the next gate run (name the lines), nothing else is switched; the first real timings come from the Clerk gate log. Report pass, blocking, evidence (every PASS/FAIL line, every pasted output), findings (the FINDING lines), timings.', { label: 'check:' + K, phase: 'Check', schema: VERDICT, agentType: 'engineer', model: 'sonnet' })
out = { ...out, check }
if (!(check && check.pass)) return { ...out, stopped: 'check:' + K }
if (check.findings && check.findings.length && !FINDINGS_OK) return { ...out, stopped: 'findings', next: 'the Check listed tests whose verdict differs alone and under --dist loadfile (check.findings): the Architect or Westley rules on each (fix the test by a test-defect row, keep it red and recorded, or change the flags); then relaunch with args.skip for the finished steps and args.findingsOk true' }
const FINDING_ROWS = (check.findings || []).join(' | ')

phase('Clerk')
const clerk = done('clerk:' + K) || await agent((LANDING ? 'LANDING RULE FOR THIS RUN (overrides section (b) where it differs): ' + LANDING + '\n' : '') + RULES + '\nRole: landing clerk (Engineer), rules.md section (b). The Dispatcher tells you at launch which landing rule applies (the temporary landing rule of dispatcher.md if it is on main). Piece ' + ROW + ' of ' + SPEC + '; tooling, no shot, no story_reviews row.' + SPEC_BLOCK + MEASURE_BLOCK + ' ' + (PUSH_MAIN ? 'The push to main at the end IS authorised on a clean gate (Westley\'s standing word for clean-gate pushes, passed by the Dispatcher), subject to the known-red rule below. AT MOST ONE LANDING IN FLIGHT: the flock below serialises it.' : 'Do NOT push to main (args.pushMain false): branch only.') + ' DEPENDS CHECK, after git fetch origin and before the lock and before any gate: git show origin/main:' + PIECES_TOML + ', read the state of ' + DEPS.join(', ') + ' (all four must be attached; HARNESS-gate-keep-red-evidence and VG-E-prodslot land first). Also read depends_on of the ' + ROW + ' row there: if it holds any of VG-CONTRACT-layerspot, VG-CONTRACT-route or LAB-REV2-E0 stop the same way with stop_reason "reversed-edge: <ids>". If any of the four is not attached on origin/main stop with ok=false, stop_reason "depends-not-attached: <ids>": take no lock, run no gate, land nothing on main, but build, run the tests and the pre-gate and push the branch ' + LB + ' with everything done except the gate, the landing edits, the records commit and the push to main; write .wt-done; say so at the top of the summary. Also check pytest-xdist imports in ' + GATE_PY + ' and ' + PY + ' (a plain check; it passes). Branch ' + LB + ', suffix vg-harness-' + K + '-land, from origin/main; merge origin/' + tests.branch + ', origin/' + build.branch + rulingMerge() + '. Stage files by name only; never a *.import or *.uid file; delete untracked .uid files before any checkout or merge. Conflicts: in ' + PIECES_TOML + ' take origin/main\'s side of every conflicting hunk (the row already carries this piece\'s owns); in ' + LEDGER + ' keep both sides; a row that appears more than once after the merge keeps one copy: drop byte-identical copies; if two copies of a row differ by any byte STOP and report the diff, never pick one. Any other conflict: STOP and report; in particular a conflict in ' + GATE_SH + ' or ' + CONFTEST + ' from another landed piece (HARNESS-gate-keep-red-evidence puts MALLOC_PERTURB_=255 on the same two statements) is never resolved by guessing: report the two sides. Run ' + NEWTEST + ' and tests/specfactory (' + PY + ' -m pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider tests/specfactory) and list PASS/FAIL per touched file: acceptance tests the gate cannot run for a comma list of pieces (the acceptance-ids and undertest steps WARN and skip: quote the WARN lines); the failing set must equal the baseline (' + ((pre.baseline_red || []).join(', ') || '(none)') + '). Pre-gate before the lock (section (b)): ' + PREGATE('<landing worktree>', 'origin/main', NEWTEST) + '; it must end OK (a lint, footprint, owner-row or noise reject is fixed or reported before the lock, never spent on a full gate). Full gate EXACTLY section (b), detached into the background from the landing worktree, the lock taken first and origin/main fetched and merged inside it (main moves while a clerk waits for the lock): mkdir -p ~/Projects/om-push/tmp-vg-harness-' + K + '; start the following in the BACKGROUND (run_in_background; the clerk waits on the lock without a timeout, flock with neither -w nor -n): flock ~/Projects/om-push/gate.lock env TMPDIR=$HOME/Projects/om-push/tmp-vg-harness-' + K + ' MERGE_GATE_SUITE_TIMEOUT=2400 MERGE_GATE_PLAYTHROUGH_TIMEOUT=2400 MERGE_GATE_PLAY_TIMEOUT=900 MERGE_GATE_PIECES=<landing worktree>/' + PIECES_TOML + ' bash -c \'cd <landing worktree> && git fetch origin && git merge --no-edit origin/main && scripts/specfactory/pre_gate.sh <landing worktree> origin/main ' + PIECES + ' ' + NEWTEST + ' && scripts/specfactory/merge_gate.sh <landing worktree> origin/main ' + PIECES + '\' >$HOME/Projects/om-push/tmp-vg-harness-' + K + '/gate.log 2>&1 (three positional arguments to merge_gate.sh; the last is ONE comma list with no spaces; add any further owner id a footprint line names and re-run the pre-gate; the pre-gate above is the cheap early check and pre_gate runs again inside the lock, on the tree after the merge; the script rejects a candidate that lacks the current origin/main, so a forgotten merge costs seconds, not a gate). Poll gate.log for the ^GATE look line with one foreground command under 10 minutes at a time, every 5 minutes at most; then pgrep -f \'^bash scripts/specfactory/merge_gate.sh\' to confirm no gate for the worktree still runs (never pgrep your own command line). There is no VERDICT line: the verdict is the set of GATE <stage> REJECT lines (and a PRE_GATE REJECT line inside the lock stops the chain: quote it); flake rule per section (b). THIS LANDING CHANGES THE GATE\'S OWN csim AND transport STAGES: its candidate-side runs use the new command (-n 5 and -n 2 with --dist loadfile), and because the command changed the baseline cache misses ("baseline: computed <sha>" in gate.log: quote it) and the baseline runs the SAME command against the base tree, whose conftest is still the old one, prebuilt by the --before-build. Quote the GATE regression_csim and GATE transport lines verbatim with their seconds (the measurement: the csim stage was about 40 minutes before; say the number you see) and the count of passed and failed they report. If a csim or transport stage REJECTS with a message naming a library path, make or COMPILE ERROR, the piece broke it: stop, branch only. The push is its OWN command, run only after you have read the verdict from gate.log: never chain git push behind pre_gate.sh or merge_gate.sh in one command line. KNOWN-RED RULE (section (b), Architect 2026-10-12): push main only when EVERY GATE REJECT line names a test or play listed by exact id in scripts/specfactory/gd_tests_known_red.txt or scripts/specfactory/lane_plays_known_red.txt on the landing tree (the Preflight quoted them: ' + (pre.known_red || '(read both files)') + '); a reject outside those files means branch only, ok=false, stop_reason "gate-reject", every REJECT line quoted, never a push. If no REJECT, or only listed ones: the landing edits are ONE separate RECORDS COMMIT on top of the merged, gated tree (normal prose, ending with the attribution line the conversation gives): in ' + PIECES_TOML + ' flip ' + ROW + ' to status = { state = "attached", attach_sha = "<sha7 of the gated merge commit, the HEAD before this records commit>" } (the format of the attached rows; comment "landed <sha7>"); ' + LEDGER + ' (PP-ledger): grep the ledger and the register for DRAFT-xdist-workers first and, if there is no hit, add one row in the ledger\'s own format with the dayNN of its last rows (day37 on 2026-10-21): "| dayNN | DRAFT-xdist-workers (named draft, harness piece HARNESS-csim-xdist) | scripts/specfactory/merge_gate.sh csim and transport stage statements | pytest-xdist worker counts of the gate: csim -n 5, transport -n 2, --dist loadfile; three stacked gates of 5 workers plus 4 lab workers are 19 on 16 cores; full gates are serialised by the flock, so it probably does not bite (Architect 2026-10-21). Architect draft, Westley owns the number. |"' + (FINDING_ROWS ? '; one more row per finding of the Check, status "finding, ruled by the Architect or Westley before this landing": ' + FINDING_ROWS : '') + '; the programme file ' + PROGRAMME + ' only if its lane table has a row naming ' + ROW + ' (HARNESS-status owns it; else say so); write nothing about status anywhere else (no ROADMAP lane row, no journal line: the commit subject is the journal); no shot, no story_reviews row: this is tooling. Right before the push: git fetch origin; if origin/main moved, merge it in (say so; ledger appends keep both sides) and re-run the pre-gate, not the full gate. Push the branch ' + LB + ', then ' + (PUSH_MAIN ? 'git push origin HEAD:main as its own command (only under the known-red rule above)' : 'stop at the branch (args.pushMain false)') + '. Write .wt-done (date, branch, pushed sha) after the push and remove the worktree only if it is clean and its HEAD is contained in origin (git branch -r --contains HEAD), else leave it with .wt-done; list the merge_gate_before_* and om_csim_* directories under your own TMPDIR first (ls), then delete each by its literal, fully written-out path (never a glob as an rm target); a gate timeout that SIGKILLs the controller leaves an om_csim_<pid> directory behind: list it in the report. The report summary carries: the stage lines verbatim ("OK per stage" or every GATE REJECT line) with the csim and transport seconds, the pre-gate verdict, the WARN lines, the test lines, main head, the records commit sha, and the plain statement of what is a stub or not done: the flags are live on the next gate run only after this landing; the worker counts are named drafts; bench_tactical_pipe.py needs a prior make; the host install of pytest-xdist is not in git. Report ok, branch, sha, summary, red_ids, stop_reason.', { label: 'clerk:' + K, phase: 'Clerk', schema: REPORT, agentType: 'engineer', model: 'sonnet' })
out = { ...out, clerk }
if (clerk && /^(depends-not-attached|reversed-edge)/.test(String(clerk.stop_reason || ''))) return { ...out, stopped: clerk.stop_reason, pushMain: false, next: LB + ' holds the piece (built, checked, pushed; nothing on main); when the dependencies named in the stop reason are attached, relaunch with args.skip for every finished step' }
if (!(clerk && clerk.ok)) return { ...out, stopped: 'clerk:' + K }
return { ...out, pushMain: PUSH_MAIN, next: 'HARNESS-gate-tiers (depends on this piece) may be built; the real csim and transport stage seconds are in the clerk summary; DRAFT-xdist-workers waits for Westley to confirm' }
